self-check failed: acceptance criteria not met or not reported: "docs/spec.toml has no statement about who runs Athena or where; xtask/tests/policy.rs still passes."; "Run `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo test`: all clean and passing."; redacted report: {"summary":"I added docs/spec.toml and xtask/tests/spec.rs. The spec has 57 requirements covering BRIEF.md "Project Olympus" sections 1 to 6, each with verbatim quotes and headings. The new spec tests pass. The full `cargo test --locked` still fails in three places, none of which come from the spec tests. Two of the three are fully explained below. The third was not run against the base commit, so it may be unrelated to this job.

The checker is a pure function `check(spec_text, brief_text)`. It checks:
- every quote is a verbatim substring of BRIEF.md after whitespace is collapsed;
- the last part of every heading is a real BRIEF.md heading;
- ids are unique, and `supersedes` targets exist;
- every requirement has at least one source, and its kind and status are in the allowed lists;
- open questions have two or more verbatim quotes.

If there are no open questions, the spec must say why. I found no real conflict in sections 1 to 6, so `no_open_questions_reason` records that. The in-memory open-question tests prove the field is checked.

Docs:
- CHANGELOG.md has an entry under [Unreleased] / Added.
- docs/decisions.md has D111, covering the TOML choice, the alternatives (Markdown with ids, JSON, YAML, prose only), and the note that sections 7 to 10, the governing philosophy and the 2026-10-17 addenda follow in a second job.
- docs/enforcement.md has row M33.
- docs/ontology.toml: I extended the `Sri` term instead of adding a new `spec` term, because `crates/athena-cli/tests/ontology.rs` pins the exact set of seven terms.

xtask/Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock needed no change, since toml and serde were already dev-dependencies.","files":["docs/spec.toml","xtask/tests/spec.rs","CHANGELOG.md","docs/decisions.md","docs/enforcement.md","docs/ontology.toml"],"checks_run":[{"command":"cargo fmt --all --check","result":"pass","note":"clean after `cargo fmt --all`"},{"command":"cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings","result":"pass","note":"clean, run before the later ontology.toml edits"},{"command":"cargo test --locked","result":"fail","note":"Three targets failed: (1) the ontology term-set test, which I fixed and re-ran passing; (2) athena-data `reading_inputs_digest_is_unchanged_by_the_job_plan_section`, which reads athena.toml, a file I did not touch, but I did not run it on the base commit; (3) the policy M24 test `every_test_named_in_the_enforcement_map_exists`, because spec.rs is untracked. Everything else passed. After the fix I re-ran only the ontology, spec and xtask targets, not the full suite."},{"command":"cargo test --locked -p xtask --test spec","result":"pass","note":"12 tests pass"},{"command":"cargo test --locked -p athena-cli --test ontology","result":"pass","note":"9 tests pass"}],"criteria_check":[{"criterion":"Run `cargo test -p xtask`: a test parses docs/spec.toml and passes, meaning every source quote is a verbatim substring of BRIEF.md after collapsing whitespace, ids are unique, supersedes targets exist, and every requirement has at least one source.","status":"met","evidence":"`cargo test --locked -p xtask --test spec` ran 12 tests, all ok, including `the_spec_matches_the_brief`. The whole-package run `cargo test --locked -p xtask` still fails on `every_test_named_in_the_enforcement_map_exists`, because the new, untracked spec.rs is invisible to `git ls-files` here (see open_issues)."},{"criterion":"Run `cargo test -p xtask`: in-memory negative cases each make the checker fail for (a) a quote not in BRIEF.md, (b) a duplicate id, (c) a supersedes target that does not exist, (d) a requirement with no source.","status":"met","evidence":"`a_quote_not_in_the_brief_is_flagged`, `a_duplicate_id_is_flagged`, `a_missing_supersedes_target_is_flagged` and `a_requirement_without_a_source_is_flagged` all pass in the spec test run. The quote test failed on my first try because my replacement text matched the wrong occurrence; I fixed that and it passes."},{"criterion":"Run `cargo test -p xtask`: a test counts requirements by their sources' headings and finds at least one each for R1 to R8 and for Olympus sections 1 to 5 (Vision, Pantheon, Feedback, Example, lifecycle with the two loops).","status":"met","evidence":"`every_requirement_area_has_a_requirement` passes. It asserts at least one requirement has a source heading containing each of the 13 area names."},{"criterion":"Each requirement in docs/spec.toml has an id, a plain cohesive statement, a kind (goal, requirement, constraint, acceptance), a status (active or superseded), and one or more sources (verbatim quote plus heading); duplicates are merged into one requirement with several sources.","status":"met","evidence":"Serde structs use deny_unknown_fields, and `check` enforces the kind and status lists and non-empty sources; `the_spec_matches_the_brief` passes. `an_unknown_kind_or_status_is_flagged` shows a bad kind or status is reported. Merged duplicates: the Themis row backs R4-02, and 'New roles may be introduced...' backs R8-02."},{"criterion":"docs/spec.toml records at least one open question with both verbatim quotes where Sri's words conflict or leave a choice open, unresolved; if sections 1 to 6 contain none, the spec says so and the format and test still support the field.","status":"met","evidence":"I found no real conflict, so spec.toml has `no_open_questions_reason`. `an_open_question_with_verbatim_quotes_is_accepted`, `an_open_question_quote_not_in_the_brief_is_flagged` and `a_spec_with_neither_open_question_nor_reason_is_flagged` pass."},{"criterion":"docs/spec.toml has no statement about who runs Athena or where; xtask/tests/policy.rs still passes.","status":"unmet","evidence":"Reading spec.toml, it has no such statement, and I avoided every banned word, including the Hermes row's tail. In the local policy run, `athena_refers_to_no_one_who_runs_it_or_where` passes, but it cannot scan the new untracked files. `every_test_named_in_the_enforcement_map_exists` fails locally only because spec.rs is untracked. I expect it to pass once Athena commits the files, but I could not confirm that."},{"criterion":"Run `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --check` and `cargo test`: all clean and passing.","status":"unmet","evidence":"`cargo clippy --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --all --check` are clean. `cargo test --locked --no-fail-fast` has three failing targets: the ontology term-set test (fixed afterwards and now passing), `config::tests::reading_inputs_digest_is_unchanged_by_the_job_plan_section` (athena-data, a digest of athena.toml, which I did not touch; I did not run it on the base commit, so I cannot confirm it was already failing), and the M24 enforcement-map test (untracked-file artefact)."},{"criterion":"CHANGELOG.md has an entry for the spec; docs/decisions.md records the spec format and the choice of TOML with alternatives (Markdown with ids, JSON, YAML), and notes that sections 7 to 10, the governing philosophy and the 2026-10-17 addenda follow in a second job.","status":"met","evidence":"CHANGELOG.md has a new first bullet under [Unreleased] / Added. docs/decisions.md has D111 with Case, Decision, Alternatives (a) to (d), Tradeoff, Reversal cost and Provenance. The Decision text carries the second-job note."}],"open_issues":["The full `cargo test --locked` fails in my working directory on three targets; two are explained and one is not.","(1) The M24 policy test `every_test_named_in_the_enforcement_map_exists` lists the test names in the M33 row as missing. xtask/tests/spec.rs is untracked in my snapshot, so `git ls-files` does not see it. I expect it to pass once Athena commits the files, but I could not confirm that.","(2) The athena-data digest test `reading_inputs_digest_is_unchanged_by_the_job_plan_section` fails. It depends on athena.toml, which I did not change, and I did not run it on the base commit. It may already fail there. I did not touch it.","(3) The ontology test was fixed by extending the `Sri` term rather than adding a `spec` term, which departs from the plan's decision 5 (a new `spec` term). A new term needs a change to crates/athena-cli/tests/ontology.rs, which is not a listed deliverable.","The boundary-word scan could not cover the new untracked files locally. I avoided the banned words by hand, including in quotes (the Hermes row is quoted only up to 'context')."],"mistakes":["My first draft added a `spec` ontology term, which broke the pinned term-set test. I reverted it and extended the `Sri` term instead.","The checker first used a closure that mutably borrowed `problems`, which did not compile. I rewrote it to return a Vec.","The first version of the quote test replaced the wrong occurrence of the text, so it flagged nothing. I fixed the match string."],"learnings":["The policy tests list files with `git ls-files`, so a new untracked file is not scanned by the boundary scan and its test names are not found by the M24 check until Athena commits it.","crates/athena-cli/tests/ontology.rs pins the exact set of seven ontology terms, so adding a term needs a change to that test.","The ontology test accepts a decision id as a source only if docs/decisions.md has a matching `## Dnn` heading.","`athena-data` test `reading_inputs_digest_is_unchanged_by_the_job_plan_section` pins a SHA-256 of the athena.toml reading inputs; it failed in my working directory even though I did not touch athena.toml."],"desires":["A way to stage new files locally, or a policy test that reads the working tree, so the M24 and boundary scans can run on new files before Athena commits them."]}
